# Cursor Rules Index

Use these detailed rules together with the cross-agent [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). Cursor loads `alwaysApply: true` rules in every session and `globs` rules when matching files are in context. Other agents should read the applicable rules explicitly. Keep both structures aligned when rules change.

## Always applied (4)

| Rule | Scope |
|------|-------|
| `chatwoot-core.mdc` | Scope, risk-based tests, naming, errors, commits, i18n (EN + fork pt_BR), branding |
| `chatwoot-dev-commands.mdc` | Setup, run, seed, lint, test, worktrees, hooks |
| `architecture.mdc` | Layers, access-control surfaces, anti-patterns, composition |
| `fork-workflow.mdc` | Branches, safe upstream sync, `custom/`, Enterprise-via-Custom, specs, hooks, FORK markers |

## File-scoped (3)

| Rule | Globs |
|------|-------|
| `ruby-conventions.mdc` | `**/*.rb` |
| `vue-frontend.mdc` | `**/*.{vue,js,ts}` (incl. async membership gates) |
| `enterprise-edition.mdc` | `{app,custom,enterprise,lib,config}/**/*.{rb,yml}` (fork extensions → `custom/`) |

## On demand (1)

| Rule | When |
|------|------|
| `pull-requests.mdc` | Opening or drafting a PR |

## Entry points

`AGENTS.md` is the complementary cross-agent entry point; `CLAUDE.md` and `.windsurf/rules/chatwoot.md` link to it and this directory. Edit implementation details here and maintain the links and shared workflow in `AGENTS.md`.
